<title>INDIA: India forex reserves rise to $26.75 bln on Apr 25.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves rise to $26.75 bln on Apr 25.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves rose to $26.75 billon on April 25, up from $26.56 billion a week ago, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.</p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  Apr 25	Apr 17	 Apr 26</p>
<p>					   1997	  1997	   1996</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     22,673	22,509	 17,242</p>
<p>    Gold				 4,054	 4,054	  4,561</p>
<p>    SDRs				    27	     2	     12</p>
<p>    Total			     26,754	26,565	 21,815</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
